  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the second of six runs: 8 witnesses, 14 names, no compositions.\n\n**What the rule says**\n- **Applies when:** the subject (a vehicle) is in a travel lane g. That lane lies on a highway w, and crosswalk c is the nearest one on w ahead along g. A warning device d (an active crossing warning signal, or a person directing traffic who shows stop) controls g. The subject has stopped at least fifty feet from c under that warning, and the warning has continued with c still ahead ever since.\n- **Ends when:** the signal goes inactive, the person shows proceed, or d stops controlling g or leaves the scene. At that point the rule no longer applies.\n- **Obligation:** the subject stays at rest (`drv_motion_complete_halt`, using `p.halt_speed_tolerance`).\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. **`WITNESS_FAIL` on `blind`.** It came out unknown because the history before the trace was missing, not because of the masked atom (`dev.governs`). I also had the scene itself leave governance unobserved, so it was unknown even with nothing masked. Fix: the guard shows proceed at the first instant, so the past is decided. Governance stays observed in the scene, and only the mask hides it.\n2. **OK.**\n\n**Choices the node left open**\n- **\"Nearest\":** c is the closest crosswalk ahead on w, measured by distance along the lane. That is the same measure the record uses for \"ahead\". Because this is a condition span, I didn't declare it as a narrowing; the rule's header comment explains it. I declared no narrowings.\n- **\"Removed / left the locality\":** a device that has left the scene no longer makes the rule apply.\n\n**Witness I added:** `branch_4` (expected not applicable). There is a nearer crosswalk, and the subject stops within fifty feet of it, though more than fifty feet from the farther one. Without this scene, nothing tests the \"nearest\" condition.\n\nEarly on I made one extra shell call (the gate command with `--help`). It was blocked and never ran, so it used no budget.\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- task_result.md",
